# Deployment Guide
## TCEA Student Cover Page Maker

This guide explains how to run, upload, update, and deploy the TCEA Student Cover Page Maker using GitHub and Vercel.

## 1. Run the Project Locally

The project does not require a backend server or additional installation.

1. Extract the project ZIP file.
2. Open the extracted project folder.
3. Locate `index.html`.
4. Double-click `index.html`.
5. The application will open in your default browser.

Recommended browsers:
- Google Chrome
- Microsoft Edge
- Mozilla Firefox

## 2. Create a GitHub Repository

1. Visit https://github.com.
2. Sign in to your GitHub account.
3. Click the **New repository** option.
4. Enter the repository name:

   `tcea-student-cover-page-maker`

5. Add a short description:

   `A free student utility for creating printable academic cover pages.`

6. Choose Public or Private.
7. Click **Create repository**.

## 3. Upload Project Files to GitHub

Upload the complete project folder structure.

Make sure the repository contains:

```text
tcea-student-cover-page-maker/
├── index.html
├── css/
│   └── style.css
├── js/
│   └── app.js
├── assets/
│   └── tcea-logo.jpg
├── README.md
└── DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md
```

You can upload files directly through GitHub:

1. Open your repository.
2. Click **Add file**.
3. Select **Upload files**.
4. Upload the project files and folders.
5. Enter a commit message.
6. Click **Commit changes**.

## 4. Update an Existing GitHub Repository

If the repository already exists:

1. Open your existing GitHub repository.
2. Select the file you want to update.
3. Open the file and click the edit option, or upload its replacement.
4. Add the updated files.
5. Commit the changes.

For a complete project update, make sure the latest versions of HTML, CSS, JavaScript, assets, and documentation are uploaded.

## 5. Deploy Using Vercel

1. Visit https://vercel.com.
2. Sign in using your GitHub account.
3. Click **Add New → Project**.
4. Find your GitHub repository.
5. Click **Import**.
6. Configure the project.

Recommended settings for this static HTML project:

- Framework Preset: Other
- Root Directory: `./`
- Build Command: Leave empty
- Output Directory: Leave empty
- Install Command: Leave empty

7. Click **Deploy**.

Vercel will build and publish your website.

## 6. Update the Live Website

If your GitHub repository is already connected to Vercel:

1. Make changes to your local project files.
2. Upload or push the updated files to GitHub.
3. Commit the changes to your connected deployment branch.
4. Vercel automatically starts a new deployment.
5. Wait until deployment is successful.
6. Open your live website and verify the changes.

## 7. Verify the Deployment

After deployment, check:

- All four cover-page templates.
- Student information fields.
- Faculty 1 displayed by default.
- Faculty 2 and Faculty 3 appearing only when requested.
- Faculty removal functionality.
- Live document preview.
- Local draft saving.
- Previously saved draft migration.
- A4 print layout.
- PDF download.
- TCEA logo loading.

## 8. Troubleshooting

**Website not updating?**
- Check whether the latest changes were committed to GitHub.
- Check the latest deployment status in Vercel.
- Refresh the website.

**Logo not appearing?**
- Check that `tcea-logo.jpg` exists inside the `assets` folder.
- Verify the image path in the code.

**CSS or JavaScript not loading?**
- Verify the file paths.
- Check that folder names and filenames match exactly.
- Check browser developer tools for errors.

**Saved drafts missing?**
- Check that browser local storage has not been cleared.
- Open the website using the same browser and origin previously used.

